Interview shortcut:

Registered domain = name, Hosted Zone = DNS records, Health Check = server health.


Registered Domain → the domain name you registered, e.g. mycompany.com
Hosted Zone → where you configure DNS records for that domain
Health Check → checks whether your application endpoint is healthy.

In Route 53 Hosted Zone, you create DNS records. Each record tells Route 53 where or how a domain should resolve.

The main record types you should know for interviews are:

Record	Meaning	Example
A	Domain → IPv4 address	example.com → 13.234.50.10
AAAA	Domain → IPv6 address	example.com → IPv6 address
CNAME	Domain → another domain name	www.example.com → example.com
MX	Specifies mail servers	example.com → mail server
TXT	Stores text/verification information	Domain verification, SPF
NS	Specifies authoritative name servers	Hosted zone name servers
SOA	Contains basic DNS/zone information	Zone's authoritative DNS information
Alias	AWS-specific routing to supported AWS resources	example.com → ALB

Easy interview memory

A = IPv4
AAAA = IPv6
CNAME = another domain
MX = email
TXT = text/verification
NS = name servers
SOA = zone information
Alias = AWS resource

